.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-egress-ips - Egress IPs of a container environment


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container egress-ips  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Egress IPs of a container environment

.PP
Current public IPv4 addresses the containers reach the internet from - add them to the IP allow list of an external service. Egress IPs of a \fBdedicated\fP environment = the public IPs of its own nodes + the shared pool node(s) used while an update rolls out (the new copy starts there for about a minute, then moves back to your node). \fBServerless\fP = the shared sandboxed pool nodes (the pool can grow: a new address can appear). Build machines of Gyro Pipeline are listed separately (\fBbuild_ips\fR). The list changes when the nodes change (plan change, node replacement, pool scaling); the owner is notified (Alerts channels, event \fBegress\fR). No IPv6 egress; outbound TCP 25 is closed. A fixed egress address is not offered yet.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-ips (operationId getContainerEgressIps, scope services_read)


